course: dictionary
lesson: 7817
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one the author means. The word quiet is a good example. «Please keep quiet during the test» means do not make a noise. In the dog advice, «stay quiet until it loses interest» means stay still and make no sound.
explain: Look at the words around quiet. «A quiet street» is peaceful, with not much happening. «A quiet boy» is someone who does not talk much. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then swap your meaning in to check it still makes sense.
explain: Quiet can also be a noun or a verb. «Peace and quiet» uses the noun: silence and calm. To quiet a noisy class means to make it quiet, which is the verb. Look at the job the word does in the sentence and the meaning follows.
fact: Quiet is an adjective when it describes a noun, as in «a quiet voice» or «a quiet street».
fact: «Quiet» means making little or no noise, as in «a quiet voice».
fact: «Quiet» can mean peaceful, with not much happening, and it can also mean not talking much or shy.
fact: As a noun, quiet means silence and calm: «peace and quiet».
fact: Phrases: «keep quiet» means stay silent; «keep it quiet» means keep it secret; «quiet down» means become less noisy.
exercise: «Please be quiet in the library.» What does quiet mean here? | *Making little or no noise | Peaceful, with not much happening | Shy and not talking much | Secret
exercise: «Kieran couldn't sleep, and the next day he went quiet in a way nobody had seen.» What does went quiet suggest? | He became very loud | *He stopped talking much, as if something was wrong | He started a club | He fell asleep at once
exercise: Which meaning of quiet fits «peace and quiet»? | *Silence and calm | Shy and not talking much | Making little noise | To make something quiet
test: «Starting a club can help quiet children find friends.» What does quiet mean here? | Making little noise | *Shy, not talking much | Peaceful | Secret
test: «Stopping screens at a fixed time, with a quiet wind-down before bed, helps children sleep.» What does quiet mean here? | Loud | Shy | *Peaceful, with not much happening | Secret
exam: «Lost cats often hide close by, quiet and scared, in sheds, garages and under cars.» What does quiet mean here? | Shy and rarely noticed | Peaceful and calm | *Making little or no noise | Keeping it secret
